{"step_index":187,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-06T17:20:04Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-06T19:20:04+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-06T19:20:04+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/Madziva/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/qualification-verification-system/docs/GIT_COLLABORATION_GUIDE.md`\nTotal Lines: 217\nTotal Bytes: 7414\nShowing lines 1 to 60\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # 🤝 Team Git & GitHub Collaboration Guide\n2: \n3: **Project:** DevOps-Enabled Qualification Verification System (QVS)  \n4: **Target Audience:** Development Team (3–5 Members) & Collaborators\n5: \n6: ---\n7: \n8: ## 📌 Table of Contents\n9: 1. [Initial Repository Setup & Pushing to GitHub](#1-initial-repository-setup--pushing-to-github)\n10: 2. [Adding & Inviting Team Members](#2-adding--inviting-team-members)\n11: 3. [Branching Strategy (GitFlow)](#3-branching-strategy-gitflow)\n12: 4. [Step-by-Step Daily Developer Workflow](#4-step-by-step-daily-developer-workflow)\n13: 5. [Pull Request (PR) & Code Review Guidelines](#5-pull-request-pr--code-review-guidelines)\n14: 6. [Managing Merge Conflicts](#6-managing-merge-conflicts)\n15: 7. [Automated CI/CD Quality Gate Checks](#7-automated-cicd-quality-gate-checks)\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## 1. Initial Repository Setup & Pushing to GitHub\n20: \n21: If the project is not yet on GitHub, the **Team Lead** should follow these steps:\n22: \n23: ### Step 1.1: Initialize Local Git Repository\n24: Open PowerShell or Terminal inside the project folder:\n25: ```bash\n26: cd qualification-verification-system\n27: \n28: # Initialize git tracking\n29: git init -b main\n30: \n31: # Stage all files\n32: git add .\n33: \n34: # Create initial commit\n35: git commit -m \"feat: initial project structure with Spring Boot, CI/CD, and docs\"\n36: ```\n37: \n38: ### Step 1.2: Create Remote Repository on GitHub\n39: 1. Log in to [GitHub.com](https://github.com).\n40: 2. Click **New Repository** (`+` icon in top-right).\n41: 3. Name it: `qualification-verification-system` (or `devops-qualification-system`).\n42: 4. Set visibility to **Public** or **Private**.\n43: 5. Do **NOT** initialize with a README, .gitignore, or license (they are already present locally).\n44: 6. Click **Create repository**.\n45: \n46: ### Step 1.3: Link & Push Local Code\n47: ```bash\n48: # Link your local repo to GitHub (replace with your repo URL)\n49: git remote add origin https://github.com/<YOUR-USERNAME>/qualification-verification-system.git\n50: \n51: # Push main branch\n52: git push -u origin main\n53: \n54: # Create and push develop branch\n55: git checkout -b develop\n56: git push -u origin develop\n57: ```\n58: \n59: ---\n60: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
